<title>Games, Games, Games! ATL-Based Auction (Ends Sun, Jan 11)</title>
<description>Hello everyone! I've got way too many games at my house and they need to go! Many were given to me by a friend who moved away, and while I've been able to find new homes for about 70% of his collection, I've still got stuff stacked up on the floors and everywhere... it's just too much! So please help me get rid of some stuff!

Rules!

1. Games will be listed with a minimum starting bid. If you're looking at possibly getting several auction items, I may be willing to let something go for a little below the minimum, but that's up to my discretion. You can reach out to me if you want to get a hint of what I'm feeling. Some games might also have a BIN price. 

2. All bids must be in whole dollars.

3. Shipping is from 30021 and will be paid by the winner, and I will ship via PirateShip with whatever is the best choice. USPS is absolutely terrible here in Georgia, so I'm likely to avoid that service. I will combine shipping if you win multiple items. If you end up with enough games, I may add some insurance, as well. Also, keep in mind that if a game is BIG and HEAVY, then the shipping might cost quite a bit. If you're worried about shipping costs, you should ask BEFORE you bid.

4. Sorry, no international bidding. If you're international and have a strong desire for an item or two, reach out to me privately and we can see if there's an option.

6. All transactions will take place via GeekMarket.

7. This auction will run until around 9 PM EST on Sunday, January 11. I will discourage sniping, so if late bids come in for something, I'll keep things open a bit longer.

8. I have lots of games, and I'm going to try to give good descriptions about the condition of everything. I will also check that everything is included in each box. That being said, I may have different criteria for games and their condition than you do. If you have high standards for your games, you need to reach out [b]BEFORE[/b] you start bidding. Don't ask about a little bit of box wear after the auction is already over and you've paid. That's silly. I will do my best to answer questions and might send pics for some games, but if you're asking 5 questions about the condition of a $1 game, you might need to look somewhere else.

9. If you have any questions, please reach out!</description>

	

